      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>The AIR Program believes in the promotion and success of American Indians within education. Via a mentoring and tutoring component, the AIR Program offers American Indians the opportunity to experiene the higher educational arena via educational workshops, library research projects, interaction with current college students, networking among college professors and community leaders, in addition to motivations and support to succeed in their post secondary school pursuits.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Semester and weekly based mentoring and tutoring for middle and high school students from the urban reservation Indian community in San Diego County. Specifically, education workshops, field trips, research projects, education counseling, and cultural based workshops.AIR Programs directely served approximatley 200 persons over the year. This includes the students, mentors, and volunteers that participated in the AIR Program services. AIR Program indirectly benefits the local American Indian community by contributing to the betterment of the Native community youth via educational motivation and cultural preservation.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
